#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407778 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d8c3ee6-fd37-5cb0-b0ab-80e7a7cca090" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454166} {:answer/id #uuid "cd824f2a-c47c-53a0-be26-c6bd74e52573" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454167}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd824f2a-c47c-53a0-be26-c6bd74e52573" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454167} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b613250-bfe0-5d10-933a-62b1f7c0e186" :answer-field/key "${v}_{1}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{2}$, ${v}_{3}$ and ${v}_{4}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454833} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e25a9185-5eae-580c-a0fe-a1704d681147" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454168} {:answer/id #uuid "0d8662e3-fc5d-5d99-afd6-2bc7152d04fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454169}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e25a9185-5eae-580c-a0fe-a1704d681147" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454168} :answer-field/id #uuid "fa4d6e3a-1748-5dc1-aec5-5bf919354400" :answer-field/key "${v}_{2}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{3}$ and ${v}_{4}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454834} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8e6560a1-a8ef-5d21-8325-256e585e4826" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454170} {:answer/id #uuid "7e317d01-b088-5a71-957d-334271a2bf38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454171}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8e6560a1-a8ef-5d21-8325-256e585e4826" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454170} :answer-field/id #uuid "528428ad-5f38-5fd7-92de-7aab58b61f83" :answer-field/key "${v}_{2}+{v}_{3}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{2}$ and ${v}_{4}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454835}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "e5252a0f-1ef3-54ce-a8b5-332d495a5706" :question/math-academy-id "q-94782" :question/problem "Consider a vector space $V$ and vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}\\in V.$ Given that ${{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}}$ is a linearly independent set and ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},\\text{ }{v}_{3},{v}_{4}}$ is a linearly dependent one, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given options in turn.\n\n- Statement “${v}_{1}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{2}$, ${v}_{3}$ and ${v}_{4}$” is true. Since ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}}$ is a linearly dependent set, we obtain that\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}+{x}_{4}{v}_{4}=0\n$$\n\nhas a non-zero solution. Moreover, ${x}_{1}$ can't be zero because then\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}+{x}_{4}{v}_{4}=0\n$$\n\nwill have a non-zero solution and that's a contradiction as ${{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}}$ is linearly independent.\nTherefore, from ${x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}+{x}_{4}{v}_{4}=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n{v}_{1}=-\\frac{{x}_{2}}{{x}_{1}}{v}_{2}-\\frac{{x}_{3}}{{x}_{1}}{v}_{3}-\\frac{{x}_{4}}{{x}_{1}}{v}_{4}.\n$$\n\nThis means that ${v}_{1}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{2}$, ${v}_{3},$ and ${v}_{4}.$\n\n- Statement “${v}_{2}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{3}$ and ${v}_{4}$” is false. Since ${{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}}$ is a linearly independent set, ${v}_{2}$ can not be a linear combination of other vectors.\n\n- Statement “${v}_{2}+{v}_{3}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{2}$ and ${v}_{4}$” is false. Since ${{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}}$ is a linearly independent set, ${v}_{3}$ can not be a linear combination of ${v}_{2}$ and ${v}_{4}.$ As a result ${v}_{2}+{v}_{3}$ can't be written as combination of ${v}_{2}$ and ${v}_{4}$ too.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${v}_{1}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{2}$, ${v}_{3}$ and ${v}_{4}$” only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407779 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34c0313d-d93b-59b9-9008-c37883836214" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407749} {:answer/id #uuid "aba7019e-307d-5b20-87e5-f4eed1088c81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The set is linearly independent" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407759} {:answer/id #uuid "e099626d-d744-5a98-9e10-eb65512f9b67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407763} {:answer/id #uuid "ee9b469b-1daa-570b-95db-cbd1983a84e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407766} {:answer/id #uuid "fea8a92c-3830-5782-841b-6499be968409" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407769}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aba7019e-307d-5b20-87e5-f4eed1088c81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The set is linearly independent" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407759} :answer-field/id #uuid "f9c05cbb-649a-584f-9952-01ecde9e3eb2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407774}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "f1e5fd69-d9bd-51e6-801e-e0af2cadcbe3" :question/math-academy-id "q-43783" :question/problem "Consider the set ${{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)}$ of polynomials from $R[t],$ where\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=2{t}^{2}+t+4,\\,{p}_{2}(t)=4t-1.\n$$\n\nIf the set is linearly dependent, find the value of $\\frac{{x}_{2}}{{x}_{1}}$ from a non-zero solution of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {p}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}\\cdot {p}_{2}(t)=0.$" :question/worked-solution "If the set is linearly dependent, then there exist ${x}_{1},{x}_{2}$ not both zero such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{p}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}{p}_{2}(t)=0.\n$$\n\nOtherwise, if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0,$ the set is linearly independent.\n\nSubstituting the given expressions for ${p}_{1}(t)$ and ${p}_{2}(t)$ into the above equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(2{t}^{2}+t+4)+{x}_{2}(4t-1) & =0 \\\\ 2{t}^{2}{x}_{1}+({x}_{1}+4{x}_{2})t+(4{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe final equation is true for every $t$ if and only if \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1} &=0 \\\\ {x}_{1}+4{x}_{2} &=0 \\\\ 4{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation we obtain ${x}_{1}=0.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we obtain ${x}_{2}=0.$ \n\nTherefore, ${{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)}$ is linearly independent."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409634 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5aaf6733-e757-5737-a6d7-d37f344e2387" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409618} {:answer/id #uuid "6536472f-623b-557c-ba85-a0b19e98cf60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409619} {:answer/id #uuid "a2ba4765-28ed-5cc7-822f-5b6db17d805d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ is not a basis of $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3},{a}_{4}}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409621} {:answer/id #uuid "f568bc4f-3c69-5e10-af38-07fcd1985ab1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409629} {:answer/id #uuid "fed87abb-5218-5d71-9132-58acdc6b2500" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409630}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f568bc4f-3c69-5e10-af38-07fcd1985ab1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409629} :answer-field/id #uuid "55d04c6b-2631-5950-abad-871e8e80ece8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409632}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "06d652ec-bdc3-5e47-8845-0d191af934f6" :question/math-academy-id "q-76334" :question/problem "The vectors ${a}_{1},$ ${a}_{2},$ ${a}_{3},$ and ${a}_{4}$ are given below. Determine whether $B={{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3},{a}_{4}}.$ If that is the case, find ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3},$ where ${a}_{4}={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}.$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{4}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -22\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We want to determine if $B$ is indeed a basis of $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3},{a}_{4}}.$ So, we want to find ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}}_{{a}_{1}}+{x}_{2}\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}}_{{a}_{2}}+{x}_{3}\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}}_{{a}_{3}}=\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -22\\end{bmatrix}}_{{a}_{4}}.\n$$\n\nThis equation is equivalent to the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{3} &=-4 \\\\ -{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-{x}_{3} &=4 \\\\ 4{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}+5{x}_{3} &=-22\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we reduce the augmented matrix of the system to reduced row echelon form (RREF):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 1 & -4 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 5 & -22\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 5 & -22\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 1 & -6\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+4{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -6\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -6\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the reduced matrix above, we see that the pivot columns are the $1$st, $2$nd, and $3$rd columns. So,  $B$ is indeed a basis of $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3},{a}_{4}}.$\nAlso, the matrix tells us that ${x}_{1}=2,$ ${x}_{2}=0,$ and ${x}_{3}=-6,$ meaning that\n\n$$\n2\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}}_{{a}_{1}}+0\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}}_{{a}_{2}}+(-6)\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}}_{{a}_{3}}=\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -22\\end{bmatrix}}_{{a}_{4}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=2+0+(-6)=-4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409635 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b9829215-b974-58e4-8c44-69d894b68143" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409623} {:answer/id #uuid "c0494c3d-162e-5780-b464-32deeb834c29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409625} {:answer/id #uuid "cbf16f8a-df5e-5944-aca2-961b097f9609" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409626} {:answer/id #uuid "dec9dd50-c1ab-549a-ab1c-6389d8a6d6c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409627} {:answer/id #uuid "f2d36c18-ea31-5abe-9c23-a6729a95f2b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409628}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f2d36c18-ea31-5abe-9c23-a6729a95f2b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409628} :answer-field/id #uuid "71a4b4a1-6fc1-55b1-954d-d7c91a2836db" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409633}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "60af0127-6c17-5939-bada-d5e4db0c560b" :question/math-academy-id "q-74970" :question/problem "Consider the vectors ${a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},$ and ${a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.$ Find a basis of $S=\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ by inspection." :question/worked-solution "Remember that a basis of $S$ is a set of linearly independent vectors that spans $S.$\n\nFrom the given vectors, we can see that ${a}_{2}$ is a linear combination of vectors ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{3}:$\n\n$$\n{a}_{2}=1\\cdot {a}_{1}+1\\cdot {a}_{3}\n$$\n\nConsequently, the vector ${a}_{2}$ can be removed from $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ without changing the span. So $S=\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ is spanned by just ${{a}_{1},{a}_{3}}.$ \n\nLastly, note that ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly independent since they are not parallel. So the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{3}}$ is a linearly independent set that spans $S.$\n\nTherefore, a basis of $S$ is ${{a}_{1},{a}_{3}},$ that is to say,\n\n$$\nB={\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}}_{{a}_{1}},\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}}_{{a}_{3}}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409636 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d2fc535-0009-527e-8e16-197236ba5926" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409616} {:answer/id #uuid "3a46ae99-d148-5f19-94ba-416fdd09e06f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409617} {:answer/id #uuid "8e0cb693-c1d6-5a53-a944-ae0f4704df17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409620} {:answer/id #uuid "b0634bb2-64a1-5d50-8b4f-34a9ef1a9df0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is not a basis of $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409622} {:answer/id #uuid "bc6282a4-c487-5b60-9f1f-e810cbeda5e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409624}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bc6282a4-c487-5b60-9f1f-e810cbeda5e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409624} :answer-field/id #uuid "065dd387-4e97-5fab-8aff-b38d1bbdcf22" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409631}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c63eedb8-35fe-5b46-b979-91cc24ab9428" :question/math-academy-id "q-76329" :question/problem "The vectors ${a}_{1},$ ${a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are given below. Determine whether $B={{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}.$ If that is the case, find ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2},$ where ${a}_{3}={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}.$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}14 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We want to determine if $B$ is indeed a basis of $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}.$ So, we want to find ${x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}}_{{a}_{1}}+{x}_{2}\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}}_{{a}_{2}}=\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}14 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}}_{{a}_{3}}.\n$$\n\nThis equation is equivalent to the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2} &=14 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} &=9\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we reduce the augmented matrix of the system to reduced row echelon form (RREF):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & -2 & 14 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 9\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -1 & 7 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 9\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -1 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the RREF matrix above, we see that the pivot columns are the $1$st and $2$nd columns. So,  $B$ is indeed a basis of $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}.$\nAlso, the matrix tells us that ${x}_{1}=2$ and ${x}_{2}=-5,$ meaning that\n\n$$\n2\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}}_{{a}_{1}}+(-5)\\cdot \\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}}_{{a}_{2}}=\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}14 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}}_{{a}_{3}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=2\\cdot (-5)=-10.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409688 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "403dcee3-3eac-5cf3-a329-0558750fb3b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409660} {:answer/id #uuid "62a1a85b-a36c-54a7-b3bd-55a36f4cb315" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409664} {:answer/id #uuid "77636ea6-fba2-560e-a69f-f3d2282f86f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409669} {:answer/id #uuid "81cdf51b-4eb6-557c-9452-11d65bc919bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409671} {:answer/id #uuid "ebe826b2-b0aa-57e0-a4ad-251af663d3fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409678}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "81cdf51b-4eb6-557c-9452-11d65bc919bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409671} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a00ccd6-15ad-566e-9909-ced57101fb7b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409684}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "4a80ad4c-5529-5931-9d7c-574d40c6f47e" :question/math-academy-id "q-72748" :question/problem "Suppose $B$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $det(B)=-7.$ The matrix $C$ is obtained from $B$ by applying the elementary row operations ${R}_{2}:=2{R}_{2}$ and ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{3}.$ What is the value of $det(C)?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's figure out what each operation does to the determinant.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{3}$ involves swapping two rows, so it changes the sign of the determinant to the opposite one.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{2}:=2{R}_{2}$ involves multiplying a row by $2,$ so the determinant is multiplied by $2$ as well.\n\nTherefore, we have to change the sign of the determinant to the opposite one and multiply by $2$ as well. Consequently, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(C) & =2\\cdot (-det(B)) \\\\  & =-2det(B) \\\\  & =-2\\cdot (-7) \\\\  & =14.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409689 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "512abaff-433d-5e4a-864f-f1df10d56d6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409663} {:answer/id #uuid "7a56edfe-4461-57d1-8804-22f3e005401a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409670} {:answer/id #uuid "f689939f-47fe-5c00-a125-9fe1fc1187ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "180" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409679} {:answer/id #uuid "face2d4d-2a2b-5eb7-8047-8fb6dbd54d8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "160" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409680} {:answer/id #uuid "fcf8031f-e31a-5703-96b3-5a28bec971aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "320" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409682}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fcf8031f-e31a-5703-96b3-5a28bec971aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "320" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409682} :answer-field/id #uuid "98c176ba-da66-551c-9c0c-0c257e4d9459" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409686}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "81c5993c-3d71-5869-bbf5-3e36b2df3a7f" :question/math-academy-id "q-72741" :question/problem "Suppose $Y$ is a $6\\times 6$ matrix and $det(Y)=5.$ What is the value of $det(2Y)?$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying a $n\\times n$ matrix by a scalar $k$ is equivalent to multiplying each row by $k,$ and this occurs $n$ times. This leads to the result\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(k\\cdot Y)={k}^{n}\\cdot det(Y).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $k=2$ and $n=6.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(2Y) & ={2}^{6}\\cdot det(Y) \\\\  & =64\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =320.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409690 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f5903e6-2dfb-5988-91aa-d76353ccd959" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409659} {:answer/id #uuid "6d3a3be9-dab5-5f7f-8e95-4eab3b47ad8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}↔{R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409665} {:answer/id #uuid "6d7bf72b-a934-51fa-b417-3e7f04a3f3b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409666} {:answer/id #uuid "7190fbd3-e0c2-5f59-a1f5-3e49c40c46d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:=2{R}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409668} {:answer/id #uuid "c8afe3f3-a5ef-55a7-b5dd-30e21d2e58fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409676}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f5903e6-2dfb-5988-91aa-d76353ccd959" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409659} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a779adf-221a-5189-a14f-312c86e15c0d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409685}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "9ac571f6-6f05-5f70-8bcf-34738f544556" :question/math-academy-id "q-43046" :question/problem "Given that $det(A)=det(B),$ which of the following elementary row operations transforms matrix $A$ to matrix $B,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 5 & -4 & -3 \\\\ 4 & 6 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 6 & 1\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since $det(A)=det(B)$, the row operation applied to $A$ must be to add or subtract a multiple of one row to another row. In other words, it is of the form \n\n$$\n{R}_{j}:={R}_{j}+(k){R}_{i},\\,i\\ne j.\n$$\n\nBy considering the given row operations that are of the above form, we notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =\\begin{vmatrix}2 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 5 & -4 & -3 \\\\ 4 & 6 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}2 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 6 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =det(B).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409691 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08098a6b-f06b-51d7-be19-39ddeb566f21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-256" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409658} {:answer/id #uuid "4da115ec-321e-53f5-9c9a-06b3818508a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409661} {:answer/id #uuid "7105bb69-b089-5e84-ab20-fd40c1edbdff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-864" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409667} {:answer/id #uuid "b58e6bc8-29ce-5a41-8721-675b80eb22cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-144" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409673} {:answer/id #uuid "fcd30542-3cc5-5b61-a9af-49753027f933" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409681}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b58e6bc8-29ce-5a41-8721-675b80eb22cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-144" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409673} :answer-field/id #uuid "04759499-638f-5548-ad9a-51762b698235" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409683}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "fded0a2c-cd1a-5de1-a671-20ea991daecd" :question/math-academy-id "q-72737" :question/problem "Suppose $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix and $det(A)=-4.$ What is the value of $det(6A)?$" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying a $n\\times n$ matrix by a scalar $k$ is equivalent to multiplying each row by $k,$ and this occurs $n$ times. This leads to the result\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(k\\cdot A)={k}^{n}\\cdot det(A).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $k=6$ and $n=2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(6A) & ={6}^{2}\\cdot det(A) \\\\  & =36\\cdot (-4) \\\\  & =-144.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411852 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "119469cb-de0c-54b8-aeed-aadcc9006b64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|A|$ and $|B|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411691} {:answer/id #uuid "52d15588-08f4-5de2-baf0-27c5fa69cb33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|A|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411721} {:answer/id #uuid "6657d1d7-2317-536b-a73c-9536580d61e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|B|$ and $|C|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411731} {:answer/id #uuid "6ba19205-12b7-5ea8-b9b0-c94f0fbef5be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|A|$ and $|C|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411735} {:answer/id #uuid "c92f219d-fedf-5abc-84b3-73dbff86703f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|B|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411787}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "119469cb-de0c-54b8-aeed-aadcc9006b64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|A|$ and $|B|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411691} :answer-field/id #uuid "1fee267d-6a43-5586-8b7a-525bf46d0281" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411822}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "0bdbb35e-75fd-595e-96b4-a35903811dc9" :question/math-academy-id "q-82288" :question/problem "Which of the following determinants are equal to $0?$\n\n$$\n|A|=\\begin{vmatrix}7 & \\sqrt{2} & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 14 & 2\\sqrt{2} & 2\\end{vmatrix},\\,|B|=\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{vmatrix},\\,|C|=\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -1\\end{vmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given determinants in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ has proportional rows: \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & \\sqrt{2} & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 14 & 2\\sqrt{2} & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|A|=0.$\n\n- The matrix $B$ has a zero row: \n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|B|=0.$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is a triangular matrix, hence \n\n$$\n|C|=2\\cdot (-3)\\cdot (-1)=6\\ne 0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $|A|$ and $|B|$ are equal to $0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411963 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1efd96de-5d59-5c21-b6c4-f57a804edb99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411913} {:answer/id #uuid "2bb7ef99-5504-5559-a251-067d58c0bd0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411914} {:answer/id #uuid "5f7847c9-3225-566d-a4bb-dbc66736309d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411923} {:answer/id #uuid "ca4dd63f-7252-5bf2-9499-144f36222c27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411945} {:answer/id #uuid "e1001e71-dfc2-59ca-a3c7-8d9e00835d22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411947}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca4dd63f-7252-5bf2-9499-144f36222c27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411945} :answer-field/id #uuid "93fee275-10ef-55f5-b6b3-8793339d38c8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411961}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "441df1fa-6b02-5f85-abd1-1592ef6dada4" :question/math-academy-id "q-72770" :question/problem "Consider the matrices given below. Given that $A$ and $B$ are row equivalent matrices and $det(A)=1$, find $det(B).$\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -8 & 12 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $B$ can be obtained from $A$ by multiplying the $2$nd row by $4.$ \n\nSo, the determinant is multiplied by $4$ as well.\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =4\\cdot det(A) \\\\  & =4\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411964 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "80e46785-3f40-5bfb-b506-ee8a0c415aa0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-31" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411931} {:answer/id #uuid "b4c18730-0551-5ec0-ac45-4897f2ad6861" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411938} {:answer/id #uuid "c3c47c2f-883c-5037-ae79-eec8f1f5feb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Undefined" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411942} {:answer/id #uuid "c5443e90-7aee-5bc1-a30a-b2f9ff32c2b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "31" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411943} {:answer/id #uuid "dcfe2730-e5ca-5dd2-b8bf-510e57549d6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411946}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c5443e90-7aee-5bc1-a30a-b2f9ff32c2b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "31" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411943} :answer-field/id #uuid "edd46d74-f62c-517b-8453-8f9197d0ad86" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411962}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "6035e308-4a34-531b-a058-679d8485fb52" :question/math-academy-id "q-130679" :question/problem "Suppose $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix and $det(A)=-31.$ The matrix $B$ is obtained from $A$ by applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{2}↔{R}_{4}$ (switching the second and the fourth rows). What is the value of $det(B)?$" :question/worked-solution "Since swapping any two rows changes the sign of the determinant to the opposite sign, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =-det(A) \\\\  & =-(-31) \\\\  & =31.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411965 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "740b596e-c7c5-57a3-a78d-d745db32ed37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411928} {:answer/id #uuid "8755e30a-6c2d-5890-9aa2-1fdaed9292a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411933} {:answer/id #uuid "99b8b3ea-b5f8-5b88-96aa-d7030872b48b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411935} {:answer/id #uuid "b4dd7187-5fd9-570d-8677-1d756d7b4a36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411939} {:answer/id #uuid "e90be040-dedb-5683-88a4-177738d9f5f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Undefined" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411949}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "99b8b3ea-b5f8-5b88-96aa-d7030872b48b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411935} :answer-field/id #uuid "92d67137-c9e6-5c58-bf53-0d6623567fde" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411960}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "8d84b0ed-254e-5487-a529-04888ae00fda" :question/math-academy-id "q-72722" :question/problem "Suppose $B$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $det(B)=12.$ The matrix $C$ is obtained from $B$ by applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{3}↔{R}_{2}$ (switching the second and the third rows). What is the value of $det(C)?$" :question/worked-solution "Since swapping any two rows changes the sign of the determinant to the opposite sign, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(C) & =-det(B) \\\\  & =-(12) \\\\  & =-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411966 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40238690-4089-5383-b0be-144e4a66318a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411917} {:answer/id #uuid "40a285bb-2c28-5dc2-bb55-500bf985bb7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411918} {:answer/id #uuid "43e91860-50ac-5b66-b967-946f1e1fc8f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411921} {:answer/id #uuid "6a51c6b8-2c73-55e3-a6ed-302213e3f577" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411925} {:answer/id #uuid "bae51b38-f76c-5484-acc5-93c339e8b199" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411940}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "40a285bb-2c28-5dc2-bb55-500bf985bb7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411918} :answer-field/id #uuid "31de2b36-2a3a-5de3-9428-2467d57745e7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411955}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "8e473584-e9d3-56ba-b273-e8476acf9443" :question/math-academy-id "q-72750" :question/problem "Suppose $C$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix and $det(C)=-24.$ The matrix $D$ is obtained from $C$ by applying the elementary row operations ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{5}$ and ${R}_{3}:=-\\frac{1}{6}{R}_{3}.$ What is the value of $det(D)?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's figure out what each operation does to the determinant.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{5}$ involves swapping two rows, so it changes the sign of the determinant to the opposite one.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{3}:=-\\frac{1}{6}{R}_{3}$ involves multiplying a row by $-\\frac{1}{6},$ so the determinant is multiplied by $-\\frac{1}{6}$ as well.\n\nTherefore, we have to change the sign of the determinant to the opposite one and multiply by $-\\frac{1}{6}$ as well. Consequently, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(D) & =-\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot (-det(C)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}det(C) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot (-24) \\\\  & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411967 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "159fb8ce-d84b-5877-8981-51153df872c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411912} {:answer/id #uuid "435012c4-9e86-5b0b-bd8c-bfd07580cbd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Undefined" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411920} {:answer/id #uuid "870e5925-34c8-51ae-b42b-4ea1fe5d0ca4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-73" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411932} {:answer/id #uuid "a73f5def-1f48-510b-8531-86b21e5603ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-103" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411936} {:answer/id #uuid "faac8cd2-8f8b-566d-bf90-337a0a3e3080" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "103" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411953}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a73f5def-1f48-510b-8531-86b21e5603ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-103" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411936} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a9f68ad-92fa-5436-8d0c-8ac0948686e5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411959}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "9e7ff967-4362-5d3c-a258-c6d91f60d8e0" :question/math-academy-id "q-130685" :question/problem "Suppose $B$ is a $7\\times 7$ matrix and $det(B)=103.$ The matrix $C$ is obtained from $B$ by applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{7}↔{R}_{3}$ (switching the seventh and the third rows). What is the value of $det(C)?$" :question/worked-solution "Since swapping any two rows changes the sign of the determinant to the opposite sign, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(C) & =-det(B) \\\\  & =-(103) \\\\  & =-103.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411968 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "116428ff-2d2f-5e28-a226-5dbcdd1ff147" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-51" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411910} {:answer/id #uuid "3fe1463d-51eb-5ce4-8cfe-2346a0890084" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "102" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411916} {:answer/id #uuid "6366fff2-1853-5bd9-92c9-a787cefc995f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-204" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411924} {:answer/id #uuid "6c822154-bc0a-542f-9975-2ec9b7c0a0cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-102" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411926} {:answer/id #uuid "c9ae59eb-ec3c-5b4c-a0c0-47d9e7c83940" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "51" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411944}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "116428ff-2d2f-5e28-a226-5dbcdd1ff147" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-51" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411910} :answer-field/id #uuid "54ea26ce-bee4-5828-891c-ff436c13a106" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411958}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "b576de71-195c-5652-8dd1-ca2db7441a59" :question/math-academy-id "q-72732" :question/problem "Suppose $B$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $det(B)=102.$ The matrix $C$ is obtained from $B$ by applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{2}:=-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2}.$ What is the value of $det(C)?$" :question/worked-solution "The row operation applied to $B$ consists of multiplying a row by the number $-\\frac{1}{2}.$\n\nWhen we do this, the determinant is multiplied by the same number. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(C) & =-\\frac{1}{2}det(B) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 102 \\\\  & =-51.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411969 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "132747fd-8145-5600-a67f-e5fedabc2538" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411911} {:answer/id #uuid "78ccb4fd-9ad3-5659-84e0-a011530ee6d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-60" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411929} {:answer/id #uuid "8b0ff215-a15d-58fa-8a84-6b3c46517368" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411934} {:answer/id #uuid "e6ee5a00-c62f-5993-8707-cb7aba8270c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411948} {:answer/id #uuid "f664b945-3527-5f51-abfc-ae17525d67b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-240" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411951}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b0ff215-a15d-58fa-8a84-6b3c46517368" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411934} :answer-field/id #uuid "2d954636-15b5-5fe0-b45f-ce012015c3e0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411954}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "befe5af1-f89b-5614-a978-2722ee7dbb46" :question/math-academy-id "q-72728" :question/problem "Suppose $X$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $det(X)=-60.$ The matrix $Y$ is obtained from $X$ by applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{3}:=\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{3}.$ What is the value of $det(Y)?$" :question/worked-solution "The row operation applied to $X$ consists of multiplying a row by the number $\\frac{1}{4}.$\n\nWhen we do this, the determinant is multiplied by the same number. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(Y) & =\\frac{1}{4}det(X) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (-60) \\\\  & =-15.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411970 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40ecf49b-f6f6-5aa8-9833-f456756fb345" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411919} {:answer/id #uuid "737d37ba-0517-586e-990a-6cb29bb74c93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411927} {:answer/id #uuid "7d6841d3-274b-5077-bf57-e479dc1150ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411930} {:answer/id #uuid "adbd9b77-9f27-5ccd-b380-119472cf1000" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411937} {:answer/id #uuid "f7b945de-5bde-5cc0-b950-21e572dcd5e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411952}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7d6841d3-274b-5077-bf57-e479dc1150ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411930} :answer-field/id #uuid "322d6374-8524-5348-bde2-7964444c576c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411956}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c64b1d7a-babf-5255-875a-51e173624ada" :question/math-academy-id "q-130734" :question/problem "Suppose $B$ is a $6\\times 6$ matrix and $det(B)=120.$ The matrix $C$ is obtained from $B$ by applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{3}:=\\frac{1}{8}{R}_{3}.$ What is the value of $det(C)?$" :question/worked-solution "The row operation applied to $B$ consists of multiplying a row by the number $\\frac{1}{8}.$\n\nWhen we do this, the determinant is multiplied by the same number. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(C) & =\\frac{1}{8}det(B) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\cdot 120 \\\\  & =15.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411971 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01085bc4-2d6b-556c-908d-a086f143e25f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411909} {:answer/id #uuid "354ead57-b818-5300-af89-ce4e85f781ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411915} {:answer/id #uuid "54a05767-12a7-5d4d-811a-9a9690b4fe5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411922} {:answer/id #uuid "bbb4c07b-c598-5d80-b49b-bf9f83404327" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411941} {:answer/id #uuid "f544947c-0c5e-5671-b370-2a270f2e40fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411950}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f544947c-0c5e-5671-b370-2a270f2e40fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411950} :answer-field/id #uuid "4855b467-0ef4-5a45-8117-ca5224a219c5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411957}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "cbb370be-de14-5258-93fd-4e6a870c68bc" :question/math-academy-id "q-72730" :question/problem "Suppose $C$ is a $9\\times 9$ matrix and $det(C)=-46.$ The matrix $D$ is obtained from $C$ by applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{9}:=-\\frac{2}{23}{R}_{9}.$ What is the value of $det(D)?$" :question/worked-solution "The row operation applied to $C$ consists of multiplying a row by the number $-\\frac{2}{23}.$\n\nWhen we do this, the determinant is multiplied by the same number. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(D) & =-\\frac{2}{23}det(C) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{23}\\cdot (-46) \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186414031 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1111935c-e645-5bcc-9a24-5310e4abf00c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414019} {:answer/id #uuid "48cbaac4-0396-5dd0-87a0-2f04eaf0760f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414022} {:answer/id #uuid "70ebcddf-aad2-5d94-849a-ae1ae9ab9ed7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414023} {:answer/id #uuid "8b765cfb-d1ea-559d-a6ff-8457bb546f81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414025} {:answer/id #uuid "979ac4ef-5db7-5cde-816c-7fb542951f8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414026}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "70ebcddf-aad2-5d94-849a-ae1ae9ab9ed7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414023} :answer-field/id #uuid "8fa000c8-106a-5c36-ab34-ed3791f10731" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414030}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "db1a0a35-4ef3-5f5a-8985-ee685a957f6e" :question/math-academy-id "q-73593" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+6y-3z &=-1 \\\\ -2x-12y+8z &=1 \\\\ -x-5y+4z &=2.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -12 & 8 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -5 & 4 & 2\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -12 & 8 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -5 & 4 & 2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -5 & 4 & 2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get ${a}_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -1\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we multiply the $3$rd row by $\\frac{1}{2}$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186414183 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c7eb0bc-15c6-5831-a79d-5637e623be55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5+3y \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414159} {:answer/id #uuid "24a55b62-4b9f-5002-bc93-434c7062356c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414161} {:answer/id #uuid "77c9e10a-76a7-504f-a64c-28abc14cbdf3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-5+3y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414171} {:answer/id #uuid "866d1061-3817-5b72-8cbe-b331346658ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5+3y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414173} {:answer/id #uuid "c85f2600-8ba5-58c2-bcb2-32e591add98e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5-3y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414176}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "24a55b62-4b9f-5002-bc93-434c7062356c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414161} :answer-field/id #uuid "3a11f4ba-4a59-5d79-a194-7e373ec165ef" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414180}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "2dc4858f-be36-5c29-9f4f-6c819c499765" :question/math-academy-id "q-20961" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+6y &=10 \\\\ 3x+9y &=21.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system." :question/worked-solution "First, we set up the augmented matrix for the system:\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & 6 & 10 \\\\ 3 & 9 & 21\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & 6 & 10 \\\\ 3 & 9 & 21\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 9 & 21\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+3y &=5 \\\\ 0x+0y &=6.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nHowever, the final equation $0x+0y=6$ has no solution. It simplifies to $0=6,$ which is a false statement.\n\nSo, there is no pair $x,y$ that satisfies both equations in the system. Consequently, the overall system has no solution."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186414184 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ee7bcb0-cbaf-5352-92b0-cd166136549a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414160} {:answer/id #uuid "4c9f17f4-9dc8-5361-a789-bdbc15bc853f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 10\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414163} {:answer/id #uuid "584317fd-30c4-5e13-a6b5-997c0e64fc09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 10\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414165} {:answer/id #uuid "5995deb2-fa58-566a-aaf9-2112bbd190f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414167} {:answer/id #uuid "80f48683-4475-5276-86de-70b5aaa6717e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414172}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1ee7bcb0-cbaf-5352-92b0-cd166136549a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414160} :answer-field/id #uuid "b7896c9b-7e0a-54c6-99f6-7e5e3f97a0cf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414182}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "66e690c7-cd96-576d-8320-9b08eb6ce160" :question/math-academy-id "q-73741" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ -5 & -10 & 5\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ -5 & -10 & 5\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -5 & -10 & 5\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186414185 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "501e28b0-b7a6-5c4a-b93c-c9142a4f1dd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2+3y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414164} {:answer/id #uuid "58b4498d-2ddc-529c-be73-05b088efbf2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414166} {:answer/id #uuid "6087853b-8e40-57de-a8a4-4d62922fe815" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2-3y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414168} {:answer/id #uuid "92f05ff5-b5f3-56d1-a8fc-bafcb1f20586" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2+3y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414174} {:answer/id #uuid "c9b78113-0b67-57ed-89a9-9f9bfbc9d657" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2-3y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414177}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "58b4498d-2ddc-529c-be73-05b088efbf2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414166} :answer-field/id #uuid "43e2c6f5-42ea-508c-b13d-901ea5805cec" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414181}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e2f37bf7-c408-5d68-a145-8a36082b4969" :question/math-academy-id "q-42163" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-3y &=2 \\\\ -12x+36y &=-28.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system." :question/worked-solution "First, we set up the augmented matrix for the system:\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ -12 & 36 & -28\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ -12 & 36 & -28\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+12{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-3y &=2 \\\\ 0x+0y &=-4.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nHowever, the final equation $0x+0y=-4$ has no solution. It simplifies to $0=-4,$ which is a false statement.\n\nSo, there is no pair $x,y$ that satisfies both equations in the system. Consequently, the overall system has no solution."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186414186 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "42e1d594-9548-59e5-aad3-072205726cc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}4-3y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414162} {:answer/id #uuid "6b96e348-3bdc-514b-ab89-33c93368576e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}3-4y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414169} {:answer/id #uuid "71d7b8c8-7f2d-57b3-ac13-87f27decfab8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414170} {:answer/id #uuid "af263a57-923f-57e9-9a38-19e80e0ea6b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}4+3y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414175} {:answer/id #uuid "e2d961c5-1118-567e-89ed-712103287b0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4+3y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414178}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "71d7b8c8-7f2d-57b3-ac13-87f27decfab8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414170} :answer-field/id #uuid "10ecc780-6036-5f50-b353-d7aef2a64027" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414179}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f4b75945-9982-5318-bfc3-2aef2116e166" :question/math-academy-id "q-42154" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x+9y &=12 \\\\ 4x+12y &=13.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system." :question/worked-solution "First, we set up the augmented matrix for the system:\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}3 & 9 & 12 \\\\ 4 & 12 & 13\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}3 & 9 & 12 \\\\ 4 & 12 & 13\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 12 & 13\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+3y &=4 \\\\ 0x+0y &=-3.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nHowever, the final equation $0x+0y=-3$ has no solution. It simplifies to $0=-3,$ which is a false statement.\n\nSo, there is no pair $x,y$ that satisfies both equations in the system. Consequently, the overall system has no solution."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415061 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c31adaa2-aedb-51ee-98cc-f5a5cb7cb242" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453874} {:answer/id #uuid "063facdd-b115-5116-95a9-caa5bdab8f25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453875}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c31adaa2-aedb-51ee-98cc-f5a5cb7cb242" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453874} :answer-field/id #uuid "a2096ae6-ffb1-5d8a-b2ca-ba762fb6d409" :answer-field/key "${x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}+{x}_{4}{v}_{4}=0$ has only zero solution ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}={x}_{4}=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454687} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3745e8da-fba3-5de6-8ee2-c06592f6933b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453876} {:answer/id #uuid "5f81960a-dd97-5893-98af-f4a31d1a3af6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453877}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f81960a-dd97-5893-98af-f4a31d1a3af6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453877} :answer-field/id #uuid "2316b283-b952-57f0-ab87-cfeeb442fa55" :answer-field/key "${v}_{2}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{1}$, ${v}_{3}$ and ${v}_{4}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454688} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "890bce99-21fe-5928-b77c-8e07e141f72f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453878} {:answer/id #uuid "8e7aea04-d3e3-5812-868c-e15e8ab20d51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453879}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "890bce99-21fe-5928-b77c-8e07e141f72f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453878} :answer-field/id #uuid "33daad36-10f5-52d9-b312-d81cb77a900b" :answer-field/key "${v}_{4}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{3}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454689}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "0c07b7ca-2c8b-5a74-a857-c6a369e5fb28" :question/math-academy-id "q-35580" :question/problem "Consider a vector space $V$ and vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}\\in V.$ Given that ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}}$ is linearly dependent and ${{v}_{1},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}}$ is linearly independent, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given options in turn.\n\n- Statement “${x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}+{x}_{4}{v}_{4}=0$ has only zero solution ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}={x}_{4}=0$” is false. Since ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}}$ is a linearly dependent set, we obtain that\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}+{x}_{4}{v}_{4}=0\n$$\n\nhas a non-zero solution.\n\n- Statement “${v}_{2}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{1}$, ${v}_{3}$ and ${v}_{4}$” is true. Indeed, solving equation ${x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}+{x}_{4}{v}_{4}=0$ for ${v}_{2},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{v}_{2}=-\\frac{{x}_{1}}{{x}_{2}}{v}_{1}-\\frac{{x}_{3}}{{x}_{2}}{v}_{3}-\\frac{{x}_{4}}{{x}_{2}}{v}_{4}.\n$$\n\nMoreover, ${x}_{2}$ can't be zero because then\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}+{x}_{4}{v}_{4}=0\n$$\n\nwill have a non-zero solution and that's a contradiction as ${{v}_{1},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}}$ is linearly independent.\nHence, ${v}_{2}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{1}$, ${v}_{3}$ and ${v}_{4}.$\n\n- Statement “${v}_{4}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{3}$” is false. Since the set ${{v}_{1},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}}$ is linearly independent set, the equation \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{3}+{x}_{3}{v}_{4}=0\n$$\n\nhas no non-zero solution. Hence, ${v}_{4}$ is not a linear combination of ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{3}$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${v}_{2}$ is a linear combination of ${v}_{1}$, ${v}_{3}$ and ${v}_{4}$” only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415475 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "045918a8-9cd8-5a07-b550-ae46024d9091" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|A|$ and $|C|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415446} {:answer/id #uuid "402ee237-56af-5ed0-b68b-15a4eb93a4c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|B|$ and $|C|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415451} {:answer/id #uuid "82c9a685-f3be-5652-9e92-444a23e21632" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|A|$ and $|B|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415458} {:answer/id #uuid "f5705fa2-288d-561a-9ae0-435e05884593" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|A|,$ $|B|,$ and $|C|$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415466} {:answer/id #uuid "fff98d8e-e1e9-59ce-9f45-62d4096f2b19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|C|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415469}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f5705fa2-288d-561a-9ae0-435e05884593" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|A|,$ $|B|,$ and $|C|$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415466} :answer-field/id #uuid "3898e8c8-305f-5107-8e55-3fa0057b225c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415470}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "135c5d03-e391-5a5b-8227-7d54c7203318" :question/math-academy-id "q-140048" :question/problem "Which of the following determinants are equal to $0?$\n\n$$\n|A|=\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1 & 0\\end{vmatrix},\\,|B|=\\begin{vmatrix}1 & \\sqrt{2} & 1 \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & 2 & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ -1 & \\sqrt{2} & 1\\end{vmatrix},\\,|C|=\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 4\\end{vmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given determinants in turn.\n\n- Since $A$ is a triangular matrix, its determinant is given by the product of the elements of the main diagonal:\n\n$$\n|A|=0\\cdot 0\\cdot 0\\cdot 0=0\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ has proportional rows: \n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & \\sqrt{2} & 1 \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & 2 & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ -1 & \\sqrt{2} & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n \nAs a result, $|B|=0.$\n\n- The matrix $C$ has a zero column: \n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|C|=0.$\n\nTherefore, $|A|,$ $|B|,$ and $|C|$ are equal to $0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415476 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "071ee791-8aa1-59a9-829e-f23787b55570" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473130} {:answer/id #uuid "be789ad4-7b1c-517c-b647-7e02fbdc4606" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473131}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "be789ad4-7b1c-517c-b647-7e02fbdc4606" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473131} :answer-field/id #uuid "1c846e82-5642-55c2-bd6c-bf9a65cc14b7" :answer-field/key "$A$ has proportional columns" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473960} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "380f5ebb-1b0a-524b-8107-7d50c50a8d0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473132} {:answer/id #uuid "2adc7349-dd06-5e86-bb35-5bbbb5b04583" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473133}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "380f5ebb-1b0a-524b-8107-7d50c50a8d0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473132} :answer-field/id #uuid "37aa9389-4822-5c22-ad9b-bf758d46df45" :answer-field/key "$A$ has identical rows" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473961} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c2322edf-ee14-5f20-8831-ec7cadfc1dd9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473134} {:answer/id #uuid "d8ca5be3-1fbc-5f41-bcbb-41b53ef5da56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473135}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d8ca5be3-1fbc-5f41-bcbb-41b53ef5da56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473135} :answer-field/id #uuid "873d7824-ac7f-5ce0-ad45-49263a39fd15" :answer-field/key "$A$ has a zero row" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473962}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "8d883981-f066-5218-a1bf-dd76574de46e" :question/math-academy-id "q-42469" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2.05 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 6 & \\sqrt{7} & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix given above. Identify **all** of the reasons why one can conclude that $|A|=0?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- $A$ has proportional columns: \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2.05 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 6 & \\sqrt{7} & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\,✓\n$$\n\n- $A$ does *not* have identical rows.\n\n- $A$ has a zero row: \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2.05 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 6 & \\sqrt{7} & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\,✓\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$A$ has proportional columns”; “$A$ has a zero row” only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415477 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "022ff781-0bb6-5222-8917-bb9fe088d40f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415445} {:answer/id #uuid "68acb0f6-b335-5e47-b870-8fcc301ed02a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415455} {:answer/id #uuid "a31adf10-60d1-51b5-9022-8cf1940c42be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415461} {:answer/id #uuid "ebaffa84-7e8a-5edc-8432-6adf9e5b2b42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415465} {:answer/id #uuid "fae22a7a-c8b8-5a0b-bb2c-5bc815b3b48d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415467}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "022ff781-0bb6-5222-8917-bb9fe088d40f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415445} :answer-field/id #uuid "d9ec239f-8a57-5ead-b4ff-042aa539477e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415472}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d4554f29-f5fb-5556-852c-2f9d95422a4d" :question/math-academy-id "q-42464" :question/problem "Find $5det(A)+7det(B)$, where \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & \\sqrt{3} & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 3\\sqrt{3} & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{3} & \\sqrt{2} & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 1 & 0 & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ 4 & 3 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- Since $A$ has proportional rows, we obtain\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & \\sqrt{3} & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 3\\sqrt{3} & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\,⟹\\,det(A)=0.\n$$\n\n- Since $B$ has a zero column, we obtain\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{3} & \\sqrt{2} & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 1 & 0 & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ 4 & 3 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\,⟹\\,det(B)=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $5det(A)+7det(B)=5\\cdot 0+7\\cdot 0=0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415478 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1859d7c5-0d55-5273-a004-f8368886466b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415448} {:answer/id #uuid "4a61a420-d52d-5f1a-b48b-ade03dffdca3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415453} {:answer/id #uuid "5fcc61bd-b9ee-5f9e-8558-651f8ea9c858" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415454} {:answer/id #uuid "851dc3ec-467b-568b-a964-3b5e34b3527e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415459} {:answer/id #uuid "e2e4e722-717d-508c-a98d-112f70b09d9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415463}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e2e4e722-717d-508c-a98d-112f70b09d9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415463} :answer-field/id #uuid "f920ea7f-06a7-52e9-8586-d0e6b44af6b3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415474}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e897ce2c-45dd-5cf3-9d25-ca84c0dd6ea8" :question/math-academy-id "q-42881" :question/problem "Find $3det(A)-det(B)$, where \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{3} & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0.57 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- Since $A$ is a triangular matrix, we have\n\n$$\ndet(A)=2\\cdot 1\\cdot 3=6.\n$$\n\n- Since $B$ has proportional columns, we obtain\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{3} & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0.57 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\,⟹\\,det(B)=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $3det(A)-det(B)=3\\cdot 6-0=18.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415479 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c54ada56-3e8b-562f-84dd-634b27dac9cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453904} {:answer/id #uuid "1bc835ea-e9b6-5ca5-a77e-0c3bd1af050b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453905}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c54ada56-3e8b-562f-84dd-634b27dac9cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453904} :answer-field/id #uuid "63c0a961-3dd4-5dcd-85e3-43b3a0493c55" :answer-field/key "$A$ has a zero column" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454702} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2456bbca-5dde-5fa3-a774-4b5dfb8431ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453906} {:answer/id #uuid "1b80c1f5-4c11-5a34-bb1a-faf5cdfce42f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453907}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2456bbca-5dde-5fa3-a774-4b5dfb8431ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453906} :answer-field/id #uuid "36456e08-b5e0-5ffb-8bc0-2e13784267ad" :answer-field/key "$A$ has two proportional rows" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454703} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5e336f47-61c7-5dfa-b071-bc593d519e33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453908} {:answer/id #uuid "05d59b93-9de5-5bdc-af50-0154b6214595" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453909}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "05d59b93-9de5-5bdc-af50-0154b6214595" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453909} :answer-field/id #uuid "0bb3bd4f-a1b2-5b23-a316-a0c1d1cd0bc3" :answer-field/key "One of the rows/columns of $A$ is a linear combination of other rows/columns of $A$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454704}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "f8a11ae3-b740-5975-a251-a4796d69b742" :question/math-academy-id "q-43307" :question/problem "Let $A$ be a $3\\times 3$ matrix such that $|A|=0.$ Which of the following statements must be true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's consider our statements in turn.\n\n- Statements “$A$ has a zero column” and “$A$ has two proportional rows” are false. For example, consider the matrix \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nExpending across the $1$st column, we have that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|A| & =1\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{vmatrix}+1\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(3-2)+(1-2) \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nbut $A$ has neither a zero column nor two proportional rows.\n\n- Statement “One of the rows/columns of $A$ is a linear combination of other rows/columns of $A$” is true. Indeed, we can make use of the following fact:\n\n$|A|=0$ *if and only if one of the rows/columns of $A$ is a linear combination of other rows/columns of $A.$*\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “One of the rows/columns of $A$ is a linear combination of other rows/columns of $A$” only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419107 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1715fd90-ec78-5246-a305-0bc79c6d6201" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419101} {:answer/id #uuid "6737f66e-5883-51c4-b5ee-f853d82f7a52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419102} {:answer/id #uuid "9beb45ed-f52f-5f55-aced-c84e6915532b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419103} {:answer/id #uuid "b56988f7-12ae-5627-bee9-3cfcc596e9cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419104} {:answer/id #uuid "ceaa277a-f8cc-5c5e-8f5b-4a33f950d108" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{10}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419105}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1715fd90-ec78-5246-a305-0bc79c6d6201" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419101} :answer-field/id #uuid "d86debef-7386-5ca7-a1b7-df6c6f4c242e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419106}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "80bf8c74-6292-5b04-9a45-fc39723fd232" :question/math-academy-id "q-73923" :question/problem "Find $m$, if $5{a}_{1}+m{a}_{2}=0$ and \n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate the $m$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{a}_{1}+m{a}_{2} & =0 \\\\ 5\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}+m\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ m\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}-5\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ m\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-30 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the first components, we get \n\n$$\n-5m=-30\\,⟹\\,m=6.\n$$\n\nBut then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-30 \\\\ 18\\end{bmatrix}\\ne \\begin{bmatrix}-30 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, there is no $m$ such that $5{a}_{1}+m{a}_{2}=0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420351 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "246b7875-4b94-5946-ab56-53b0efdaa23b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|A|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420334} {:answer/id #uuid "545d8b36-38e5-559e-a61d-ce2a27111cbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|A|,$ $|B|,$ and $|C|$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420339} {:answer/id #uuid "583e2bd2-06b9-53e2-a4b9-5c8a9049a9c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|B|$ and $|C|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420340} {:answer/id #uuid "6272e38a-2afb-598f-b018-441d73a31140" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|A|$ and $|C|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420341} {:answer/id #uuid "e5b9947c-9286-555b-9fb9-6a06456c5033" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|A|$ and $|B|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420346}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "545d8b36-38e5-559e-a61d-ce2a27111cbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|A|,$ $|B|,$ and $|C|$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420339} :answer-field/id #uuid "916484e9-1c80-5d3a-8194-ccf0b63cf5fb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420349}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "2642af15-1045-5d0f-97c1-3ce034155f08" :question/math-academy-id "q-82285" :question/problem "Which of the following determinants are equal to $0?$\n\n$$\n|A|=\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 5 & \\sqrt{3} & 5 \\\\ 0 & 8 & -1 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{vmatrix},\\,|B|=\\begin{vmatrix}6 & \\sqrt{7} & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -1\\end{vmatrix},\\,|C|=\\begin{vmatrix}6 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -\\sqrt{2} & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{vmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given determinants in turn. \n\n- The matrix $A$ has identical columns: \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 5 & \\sqrt{3} & 5 \\\\ 0 & 8 & -1 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|A|=0.$\n\n- The matrix $B$ has identical rows: \n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & \\sqrt{7} & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|B|=0.$\n\n- The matrix $C$ has a zero row: \n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -\\sqrt{2} & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|C|=0.$\n\nTherefore, $|A|,$ $|B|,$ and $|C|$ are equal to $0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420352 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "52a1dbcb-127d-567f-b362-0ca0b1d54e42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420338} {:answer/id #uuid "748fa6b4-08c9-57b1-9c5f-ace131b66c19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420342} {:answer/id #uuid "76cec32a-c27c-5e6c-94e2-bb27825747c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420343} {:answer/id #uuid "b70ba875-07c9-5c3f-85df-154df641f91f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420345} {:answer/id #uuid "ec20d6e5-b2d8-5e04-b68d-e1fd68f53231" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420347}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b70ba875-07c9-5c3f-85df-154df641f91f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420345} :answer-field/id #uuid "ff922856-e3c4-5b40-8d0e-cd85fae942ae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420350}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "89fae1b5-1405-51b4-b87d-75b6acbbdc2e" :question/math-academy-id "q-82192" :question/problem "Find $7det(A)-2det(B)$, where \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1 & 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -0.5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- Since $A$ has two identical columns, we obtain\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1 & 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\,⟹\\,det(A)=0.\n$$\n\n- Since $B$ is a triangular matrix, its determinant is given by the product of the elements of the main diagonal: \n\n$$\ndet(B)=3\\cdot (-1)\\cdot 1\\cdot 2=-6\n$$\n\nTherefore, $7det(A)-2det(B)=7\\cdot 0-2\\cdot (-6)=12.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420353 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8345ca2e-07d0-5694-85e8-8ac1bcfa3d94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474822} {:answer/id #uuid "b5ff36f5-8430-54a9-bec5-2cc165a0f1ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474823}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8345ca2e-07d0-5694-85e8-8ac1bcfa3d94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474822} :answer-field/id #uuid "df50f4aa-1524-57d2-b1e7-0affdd885093" :answer-field/key "$A$ has identical rows" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475337} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "902e3414-ca2a-5ce2-850b-da2dc63be023" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474824} {:answer/id #uuid "4e173f75-196d-539f-971b-b9d002b2252d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474825}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "902e3414-ca2a-5ce2-850b-da2dc63be023" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474824} :answer-field/id #uuid "f4a68604-a5fe-5780-aff3-ee5e03c398ad" :answer-field/key "$A$ has proportional columns" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475338} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c276a60-9989-5c94-9ab0-70747f4dd816" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474826} {:answer/id #uuid "50bacac0-c323-5e20-9449-31c6507754e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474827}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "50bacac0-c323-5e20-9449-31c6507754e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474827} :answer-field/id #uuid "affe140d-4863-54d4-bd0d-1629fd85f31c" :answer-field/key "$A$ has a zero row" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475339}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "d2486be8-75b8-51f1-882e-08f8a79961f2" :question/math-academy-id "q-42463" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 6 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix given above. Identify **all** of the reasons why one can conclude that $|A|=0?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- $A$ does *not* have identical rows.\n\n- $A$ does *not* have proportional columns.\n\n- $A$ has a zero row: \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 6 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\,✓\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$A$ has a zero row” only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420713 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19ddf127-9fb5-5724-b669-1d5d25a58040" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The set is linearly independent" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420707} {:answer/id #uuid "37daef1d-9729-5a8c-96e9-3c9478596dc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420708} {:answer/id #uuid "561c2f0d-be65-5b74-80cb-c4d610f62978" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420709} {:answer/id #uuid "7107938f-dc39-590b-a878-c6a64a6afe0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420710} {:answer/id #uuid "7e6ca647-3da8-59df-a01b-f1f1276bf3fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420711}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "19ddf127-9fb5-5724-b669-1d5d25a58040" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The set is linearly independent" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420707} :answer-field/id #uuid "f41fca13-4375-5dd3-80b4-d2dbcf42196f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420712}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "0b9ee9fe-348f-5bee-8c67-e9425237ec58" :question/math-academy-id "q-35759" :question/problem "Consider the set of matrices ${A,B,C},$ where \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -5\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -4 \\\\ 20 & -12\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 5 \\\\ -7 & -5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n \nIf the set is linearly dependent, find the value of $\\frac{{x}_{1}}{{x}_{2}}$ from a non-zero solution of ${x}_{1}A+{x}_{2}B+{x}_{3}C=O,$ where $O$ is the $2\\times 2$ zero-matrix." :question/worked-solution "If the set is linearly dependent, then there exist ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}$ not all zero such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}A+{x}_{2}B+{x}_{3}C=O.\n$$\n\nOtherwise, if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0,$ the set is linearly independent.\n\nSubstituting the matrices $A,$ $B,$ and $C$ into the above equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -5\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -4 \\\\ 20 & -12\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{3}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 5 \\\\ -7 & -5\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} & 0 \\\\ 2{x}_{1} & -5{x}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -4{x}_{2} \\\\ 20{x}_{2} & -12{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}4{x}_{3} & 5{x}_{3} \\\\ -7{x}_{3} & -5{x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}+4{x}_{3} & -4{x}_{2}+5{x}_{3} \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+20{x}_{2}-7{x}_{3} & -5{x}_{1}-12{x}_{2}-5{x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding entries, we obtain the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+4{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ -4{x}_{2}+5{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+20{x}_{2}-7{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ -5{x}_{1}-12{x}_{2}-5{x}_{3} &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we consider the corresponding augmented matrix and reduce it to row echelon form using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 20 & -7 & 0 \\\\ -5 & -12 & -5 & 0\\end{array}\\right] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+5{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 20 & -15 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -12 & 15 & 0\\end{array}\\right] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+5{R}_{2} \\\\ {R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+(-3){R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 10 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe pivot columns are  the $1$st,  $2$nd and $3$rd. Therefore, we get the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+4{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ -4{x}_{2}+5{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ 10{x}_{3} &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhich has only the zero solution ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$\n\nConsequently, ${A,B,C}$ is linearly independent."}]}
